<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="act_inst_roc_depth_of_water">
        <title>Instantaneous Rate of Change of Depth</title>
        <objectives>
                <ul>
                        <li>
                                <p>
                                        In this activity, we will continue using the conical water
                                        tank as we develop our understanding of instantaneous rates
                                        of change.
                                </p>
                        </li>
                </ul>
        </objectives>
        <introduction>
                <p>
                The first few exercises in this activity will investigate a useful algebraic
                pattern/identity that we will use fairly often throughout the course. Then, we will return to the function we developed in <xref ref="act_depth_of_water" /> and use the algebraic identity to calculate the instantaneous rate of change of depth at various times.
                </p>

        </introduction>

        <exercise workspace="1in">
                <introduction>
                        <p>
                                        Many of us are aware of the algebraic identity used for factoring a difference of squares, <m>(x^{2}-y^{2})=(x-y)(x+y)</m>, but you may not be aware that it is a special case of a much more general pattern.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                                You may find it useful in the following exercises to use an <q>area model</q> array for multiplying polynomials. For example, to multiply <m>(x-y)(x^{2}+3x y+y^{2})</m>, I could use a model as follows:
                                <md>
                                        \begin{array}{r|lll}
                                          &amp;\php{}x^{2} &amp;+3x y      &amp;+y^{2} \\ \hline
                                        x &amp;\php{}x^{3} &amp;+3x^{2}y  &amp;+x y^{2} \\
                                        -y&amp;-x^{2}y     &amp;-3x y^{2}  &amp;-y^3
                                        \end{array}
                                </md>
                        </p>
                        <p>
                                        Collecting like terms (which lie along diagonals), we see that <m>(x-y)(x^{2}+3x y+y^{2})=x^{3}+2x^{2}y-2x y^{2}-y^{3}</m>.
                        </p>
                </introduction>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                        <p>
                                        Calculate <m>(x-y)(x^{2}+x y+y^{2})</m>.
                        </p>
                        </statement>
                        <answer>
                                <p>
                                        <m>x^{3}-y^{3}</m>
                                </p>
                        </answer>
                        <solution>
                                <p>
                                <md>
                                        \begin{array}{r|lll}
                                          &amp;\php{}x^{2} &amp;+x y      &amp;+y^{2} \\ \hline
                                        x &amp;\php{}x^{3} &amp;+x^{2}y  &amp;+x y^{2} \\
                                        -y&amp;-x^{2}y     &amp;-x y^{2}  &amp;-y^3
                                        \end{array}
                                </md>
                                </p>
                        </solution>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                        <p>
                                        Calculate <m>(x-y)(x^{3}+x^{2}y+x y^{2}+y^{3})</m>.
                        </p>
                        </statement>
                        <answer>
                                <p>
                                        <m>x^{4}-y^{4}</m>
                                </p>
                        </answer>
                        <solution>
                                <p>
                                <md>
                                        \begin{array}{r|llll}
                                          &amp;\php{}x^{3} &amp;+x^{2}y      &amp;+x y^{2}     &amp;+y^{3}  \\ \hline
                                        x &amp;\php{}x^{4} &amp;+x^{3}y      &amp;+x^{2}y^{2} &amp;+x y^{3} \\
                                        -y&amp;-x^{3}y     &amp;-x^{2}y^{2}  &amp;-x y^3       &amp;-y^{4}
                                        \end{array}
                                </md>
                                </p>
                        </solution>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                        <p>
                                        Calculate <m>(x-y)(x^{4}+x^{3}y+x^{2}y^{2}+x y^{3}+y^{4})</m>.
                        </p>
                        </statement>
                        <answer>
                                <p>
                                        <m>x^{5}-y^{5}</m>
                                </p>
                        </answer>
                        <solution>
                                <p>
                                <md>
                                        \begin{array}{r|lllll}
                                          &amp;\php{}x^{4}  &amp;+x^{3}y      &amp;+x^{2}y^{2} &amp;+x y^{3}     &amp;+y^{4}  \\ \hline
                                        x &amp;\php{}x^{5}  &amp;+x^{4}y      &amp;+x^{3}y^{2} &amp;+x^{2}y^{3} &amp;+x y^{4} \\
                                        -y&amp;     -x^{4}y &amp;-x^{3}y^{2}  &amp;-x^{2}y^3   &amp;-x y^{4}     &amp;-y^{5}
                                        \end{array}
                                </md>
                                </p>
                        </solution>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                        <p>
                                        Let <m>n</m> be some (arbitrary) integer (greater than 4). Based on your previous results, what do you think would be the result of calculating <m>(x-y)(x^{n}+x^{n-1}y+x^{n-2}y^{2}+\cdots+x y^{n-1}+y^{n})</m>?
                        </p>
                        </statement>
                        <answer>
                                <p>
                                        <m>x^{n+1}-y^{n+1}</m>
                                </p>
                        </answer>
                        <solution>
                                <p>
                                <md>
                                        \begin{array}{r|lllllll}
                                          &amp;\php{}x^{n}  &amp;+x^{n-1}y    &amp;+x^{n-2}y^{2} &amp;+\cdots&amp;+x y^{n-1}     &amp;+y^{n}  \\ \hline
                                        x &amp;\php{}x^{n+1}&amp;+x^{n}y      &amp;+x^{n-1}y^{2} &amp;+\cdots&amp;+x^{2}y^{n-1} &amp;+x y^{n} \\
                                        -y&amp;     -x^{n}y &amp;-x^{n-1}y^{2}&amp;-x^{n-2}y^{3} &amp;+\cdots&amp;-x y^{n}     &amp;-y^{n+1}
                                        \end{array}
                                </md>
                                </p>
                        </solution>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                        <p>
                                        Use your previous results, making appropriate substitutions, to calculate
                                        <m>\left(b^{1/3}-a^{1/3}\right)\left(b^{2/3}+b^{1/3}a^{1/3}+a^{2/3}\right)=\left(b^{1/3}-a^{1/3}\right)\left((b^{1/3})^{2}+(b^{1/3})(a^{1/3})+(a^{1/3})^{2}\right)</m>.
                        </p>
                        </statement>
                        <answer>
                                <p>
                                        <m>b-a</m>
                                </p>
                        </answer>
                        <solution>
                                <p>
                                <md>
                                        \begin{array}{r|lll}
                                          &amp;\php{}\left(b^{1/3}\right)^{2} &amp;+\left(b^{1/3}\right)\left(a^{1/3}\right)      &amp;+\left(a^{1/3}\right)^{2} \\ \hline
                                        \left(b^{1/3}\right) &amp;\php{}\left(b^{1/3}\right)^{3} &amp;+\left(b^{1/3}\right)^{2}\left(a^{1/3}\right)  &amp;+\left(b^{1/3}\right)\left(a^{1/3}\right)^{2} \\
                                        -\left(a^{1/3}\right)&amp;-\left(b^{1/3}\right)^{2}\left(a^{1/3}\right)     &amp;-\left(b^{1/3}\right)\left(a^{1/3}\right)^{2}  &amp;-\left(a^{1/3}\right)^3
                                        \end{array}
                                </md>
                                </p>
                        </solution>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                        <p>
                                        Based on previous results, what could you multiply <m>b^{1/4}-a^{1/4}</m> by in order to obtain <m>b-a</m> as the product?
                        </p>
                        </statement>
                        <answer>
                                <p>
                                        <m>b^{3/4}+b^{1/2}a^{1/4}+b^{1/4}a^{1/2}+a^{3/4}</m>
                                </p>
                        </answer>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                        <p>
                                        Use your previous results, making appropriate substitutions, to calculate
                                        <m>\left(\left(kb+c\right)^{1/3}-\left(ka+c\right)^{1/3}\right)\left(\left(kb+c\right)^{2/3}+\left(kb+c\right)^{1/3}\left(ka+c\right)^{1/3}+\left(ka+c\right)^{2/3}\right)</m>.
                        </p>
                        </statement>
                        <answer>
                                <p>
                                        <m>\left(kb+c\right)-\left(ka+c\right)=k(b-a)</m>
                                </p>
                        </answer>
                        <solution>
                                <p>
                                <md>
                                        \small\textstyle
                                        \begin{array}{r|lll}
                                          &amp;\php{}\left(\left(kb+c\right)^{1/3}\right)^{2} &amp;+\left(\left(kb+c\right)^{1/3}\right)\left(\left(ka+c\right)^{1/3}\right)      &amp;+\left(\left(ka+c\right)^{1/3}\right)^{2} \\ \hline
                                        \left(\left(kb+c\right)^{1/3}\right) &amp;\php{}\left(\left(kb+c\right)^{1/3}\right)^{3} &amp;+\left(\left(kb+c\right)^{1/3}\right)^{2}\left(\left(ka+c\right)^{1/3}\right)  &amp;+\left(\left(kb+c\right)^{1/3}\right)\left(\left(ka+c\right)^{1/3}\right)^{2} \\
                                        -\left(\left(ka+c\right)^{1/3}\right)&amp;-\left(\left(kb+c\right)^{1/3}\right)^{2}\left(\left(ka+c\right)^{1/3}\right)     &amp;-\left(\left(kb+c\right)^{1/3}\right)\left(\left(ka+c\right)^{1/3}\right)^{2}  &amp;-\left(\left(ka+c\right)^{1/3}\right)^3
                                        \end{array}
                                </md>
                                </p>
                        </solution>
                </task>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="exer_inst_roc_depth_5">
                <introduction>
                        <p>
                                        In the exercise, we will make use of the algebraic techniques we have developed to calculate the instantaneous rate of change for the function <m>f(t)=\sqrt[3]{0.54t+8}=\left({0.54t+8}\right)^{1/3}</m>
                        </p>
                </introduction>
                <task xml:id="task_diff_quot_depth_5">
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                                Write the difference quotient <m>\frac{f(b)-f(5)}{b-5}</m>.
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                        <answer>
                                <p>
                                        <m>\frac{\left({0.54b+8}\right)^{1/3}-\left({0.54\cdot5+8}\right)^{1/3}}{b-5}</m>
                                </p>
                        </answer>
                </task>
                <task xml:id="task_depth_5_multiplier">
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                                Find an appropriate expression so that 
                                        <md>
                                                <mrow>
                                                        \left(\left({0.54b+8}\right)^{1/3}-\left({0.54\cdot5+8}\right)^{1/3}\right)\left(\text{\ldots ? \ldots}\right)\amp=(0.54b+8)-(0.54\cdot5+8)
                                                </mrow>
                                                <mrow>
                                                        \amp=0.54(b-5)
                                                </mrow>
                                        </md>
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                        <answer>
                                <p>
                                        <m>\left({0.54b+8}\right)^{2/3}+\left({0.54b+8}\right)^{1/3}\left({0.54\cdot 5+8}\right)^{1/3}+\left({0.54\cdot 5+8}\right)^{2/3}</m>
                                </p>
                        </answer>
                </task>
                <task xml:id="task_all_but_b_equal_zero">
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                                Multiply the numerator and denominator of the difference quotient in <xref ref="task_diff_quot_depth_5" /> by the expression you found in <xref ref="task_depth_5_multiplier" /> and simplify the numerator.
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                        <answer>
                                <p>
                                        <md>
                                                        \frac{0.54(b-5)}{(b-5)\left(\left({0.54b+8}\right)^{2/3}+\left({0.54b+8}\right)^{1/3}\left({0.54\cdot 5+8}\right)^{1/3}+\left({0.54\cdot 5+8}\right)^{2/3}\right)}
                                        </md>
                                </p>
                        </answer>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                                Note that for any <m>b\neq{}5</m>, <m>(b-5)\neq{}0</m>, and so <m>\frac{(b-5)}{(b-5)}=1</m>. Therefore, for every <m>b</m> except <m>b=5</m>, your expression in <xref ref="task_all_but_b_equal_zero"/> is identical to the same expression with the <m>(b-5)</m> in the numerator canceled by the <m>(b-5)</m> in the denominator, and therefore their limits as <m>b\to 5</m> are identical.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                                However, the expression with <m>(b-5)</m> canceled is continuous at <m>b=5</m> and so its limit as <m>b\to 5</m> is simply its value <em>at</em> <m>b=5</m>.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                        Evaluate this limit, and thus calculate
                                        <md>\lim_{b\to 5}\frac{f(b)-f(5)}{b-5}</md>.
                                                This is the <em>instantaneous rate of change</em> for <m>f</m> at <m>t=5</m>.
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                </task>
        </exercise>
        <exercise>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                                Repeat <xref ref="exer_inst_roc_depth_5"/> for <m>\frac{f(b)-f(2)}{b-2}</m> to find <m>\displaystyle\lim_{b\to 2}\frac{f(b)-f(2)}{b-2}</m>.
                                </p>
                        </statement>
        </exercise>
        <exercise>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                                Repeat <xref ref="exer_inst_roc_depth_5"/> for <m>\frac{f(b)-f(0)}{b-0}</m> to find <m>\displaystyle\lim_{b\to 0}\frac{f(b)-f(0)}{b-0}</m>.
                                </p>
                        </statement>
        </exercise>
        <exercise>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                                Repeat <xref ref="exer_inst_roc_depth_5"/> for <m>\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}</m> to find <m>\displaystyle\lim_{b\to a}\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}</m>, where <m>a</m> is an unspecified value.
                                </p>
                        </statement>
        </exercise>
</worksheet>
